  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "This package is provided as a .NET Standard 2.0 class library.\n\n      New in version 3.1.58\n            \n      - Push notifications now enable web sockets by default.\n            \n      Version 3.1.57\n            \n      - Device registration methods added to library.\n\n      Version 3.1.55\n\n      - Added trace logging.\n      \n      Version 3.1.52\n\n      - Updated etherFAX logo, copyright, etc.\n\n      Version 3.1.51\n\n      - Added CaptureFax and CaptureFaxAsync functions.\n\n      Version 3.1.50:\n\n      - Fixed API culture versioning issue.\n\n      Version: 3.1.49:\n\n      - StartPushLlistener method now supports useWebSockets parameter.\n      - Starting push listener will now log networking exceptions during initialization.\n\n      Version 3.1.45:\n\n      - ImageHelper.GetPageCount() now supports PDF files.\n\n      Version 3.1.44:\n\n      - Updatated Microsoft logging extensions to reference earlier version (resolve compatibility issues).\n\n      Version: 3.1.43:\n\n      - Licensing information is now provided in account status methods.\n\n      Version: 3..42:\n\n      - Default request headers can now be accessed using the DefaultRequestHeaders property.\n\n      Version: 3.1.38:\n\n      - Optional site ID can now be set when marking fax received.\n\n      Version 3.1.34:\n\n      - AnalyzeError added to AnalyzeResult response.\n\n      Version 3.1.33:\n\n      - etherFAX AI forms recognizer and data extraction services now supported.\n\n      Version 3.0.30:\n\n      - CoverPageParams is now supported.\n      - ServiceProperties is now supported.\n\n      Version 3.0.29:\n\n      - When sending a fax, the TZ value is now set automatically (if unspecified).\n\n      Version 3.0.28:\n\n      - Added ILogger to EtherFaxClient for logging/debugging.\n      - Added logger output for errors.\n\n      Version 3.0.23:\n\n      - Added class EtherFax.Enrollment to provide device self-enrollment and registration functions.\n      - Corrected signaling issue with push-notification event handling.\n      - EtherFax.Client now supports ILogger interface.\n\n      Version 3.0.20:\n\n      - Device status and enrollment functions added.",
